Patch to upstream OpenCV: make the generated bindings compile for the cv::mcc classes.

The generated bindings.cpp refers to classes by their unqualified names and relies on the
`using namespace` lines and typedefs at the top of core_bindings.cpp. cv::aruco has them;
cv::mcc (merged from opencv_contrib in 5.0) does not, and cv::dnn::Net has no dnn_Net
typedef. Upstream never noticed because its whitelist spells the mcc classes wrongly
(mcc_CheckerDetector instead of mcc_CCheckerDetector), so the generator skipped them.
src/config/opencv_js.config.py uses the real names, which needs these two lines.

The create(const dnn::Net&) overload of CCheckerDetector compiles but stays unusable:
dnn has no JS bindings in this build, so calling it throws UnboundTypeError.

Applied by build/build.sh after cloning the source; a patch that no longer applies fails
the build.

--- a/modules/js/src/core_bindings.cpp
+++ b/modules/js/src/core_bindings.cpp
@@ -91,12 +91,14 @@ using namespace cv::segmentation;  // FIXIT
 
 #ifdef HAVE_OPENCV_OBJDETECT
 using namespace cv::aruco;
+using namespace cv::mcc;
 typedef aruco::DetectorParameters aruco_DetectorParameters;
 typedef QRCodeDetectorAruco::Params QRCodeDetectorAruco_Params;
 #endif
 
 #ifdef HAVE_OPENCV_DNN
 using namespace cv::dnn;
+typedef dnn::Net dnn_Net;
 #endif
 
 #ifdef HAVE_OPENCV_FEATURES
